From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: mzak <mzak.amin@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 18 Oct 2026 12:00:00 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: qcom: kaanapali-oneplus-iceland: no placeholder
 Bluetooth address

The Bluetooth node carried a fixed local-bd-address, a value shared by
every unit. The WCN7860 reports the address of its NVM file, so btqca
sets HCI_QUIRK_USE_BDADDR_PROPERTY and the core programs the device
tree value: the controller came up configured on the shared value, and
when userspace did not manage to set the unit's own address in time
bluetoothd used it (a new adapter directory, the pairings missing).

Use an all-zero value instead. The core ignores an all-zero property,
so the controller registers as unconfigured (MGMT reports the missing
public-address option) and becomes configured only once the unit's own
address is set, either by a boot loader that fills the property or by
Set Public Address from userspace (iceland-bdaddr v3 of iceland-device
0.28-26, which must be installed first). "Bluetooth: qca: check the
device address on every setup" (queue 0261) keeps the quirk on every
later setup, so the address set once is programmed again at every
power on.

Signed-off-by: mzak <mzak.amin@gmail.com>
Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/kaanapali-oneplus-iceland.dts | 9 ++++++++-
 1 file changed, 8 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/kaanapali-oneplus-iceland.dts b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/kaanapali-oneplus-iceland.dts
index 64589cbb4dfc..226050e78304 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/kaanapali-oneplus-iceland.dts
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/kaanapali-oneplus-iceland.dts
@@ -2428,7 +2428,14 @@
 	bluetooth {
 		compatible = "qcom,wcn7860-bt";
 
-		local-bd-address = [ 25 00 00 00 5a ad ];
+		/*
+		 * All zero: filled by the boot loader when it knows the unit's
+		 * address; otherwise the controller registers unconfigured
+		 * (btqca sets HCI_QUIRK_USE_BDADDR_PROPERTY because the chip
+		 * reports its NVM default) until userspace sets the public address,
+		 * so no shared placeholder address is ever used.
+		 */
+		local-bd-address = [ 00 00 00 00 00 00 ];
 
 		vddrfacmn-supply = <&vreg_pmu_rfa_cmn>;
 		vddaon-supply = <&vreg_pmu_aon_0p59>;
